##########################################################################
# CSharpPackage-RepositoryMonitors.otter
#
# Purpose : Define BuildMaster Repository Monitors that trigger the
#           CSharpPackage-5Stage plan for the ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId
#           pilot package when matching branches are pushed in the
#           ATAP.Utilities GitHub repository.
#
# Immutable build note:
#   Under the immutable build strategy, only sprint-branch and main pushes
#   trigger pipeline runs. Tier promotion happens via BuildMaster pipeline
#   stage progression and `Promote-ProGetPackage` API calls, not branch
#   pushes to integration/qa/release branches.
#
# How to apply:
#   1. In the BuildMaster UI, open the ATAP.Utilities-CSharp application.
#   2. Navigate to Settings → Repository Monitors.
#   3. Create one monitor per entry below (or use the BuildMaster API
#      with the /api/resource-monitors endpoint).
#   4. Confirm each monitor by performing a test push to the target branch.
#
# Scaling beyond the pilot package:
#   The C# BuildMaster application is intentionally shared by package. Each
#   repository monitor must therefore provide the concrete package tuple as
#   build variables. To onboard another package, copy these two monitor entries,
#   change the monitor names, PathFilter, MetaPackageName, PackageName,
#   ProjectPath, and SolutionPath to that package.
#
# Tier resolution:
#   NBGV prerelease label → Tier → Feed
#   -Sprint-  → Experimental  → nuget-experimental
#   -Alpha-   → Development   → nuget-development
#   -Beta-    → Integration   → nuget-integration
#   -QA-      → QA            → nuget-qa
#   (none)    → Production    → nuget-stable
#
# Path filter:
#   PathFilter scopes the pilot monitors to the StronglyTypedId source tree so
#   a source push supplies one unambiguous C# package tuple.
#
# Webhook secret (1.4-3):
#   WebhookSecret references env var BUILDMASTER_GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET.
#   PREREQUISITE: Create a Bitwarden secure-note named
#     "BUILDMASTER_GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET" and add it to LoginScript.ps1 so
#     the env var is populated before BuildMaster starts.
#
# Variables used by triggered builds:
#   $Branch          — the branch that triggered the monitor (injected by BM)
#   $ApplicationName — supplied by these monitor definitions
#   $MetaPackageName — supplied by these monitor definitions
#   $PackageName     — supplied by these monitor definitions
#   $ProjectPath     — supplied by these monitor definitions
#   $SolutionPath    — supplied by these monitor definitions
#   $Configuration   — supplied by these monitor definitions
#   $SourcePath      — set as Application Variable: working-directory path
#   $ProGetUrl       — set as Application Variable: ProGet base URL
#   ProGet API key   — runner receives only ProGet.BuildMaster.API.Key as a SecretName
##########################################################################

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pilot package values
#   ApplicationName : ATAP.Utilities
#   MetaPackageName : ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId
#   PackageName     : ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId
#   ProjectPath     : src/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId.csproj
#   SolutionPath    : ATAP.Utilities.Production.slnf
#   Configuration   : Release

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monitor 1 — main branch
# Triggers  : any push to "main"
# Ceiling   : resolved from the package's version.json prerelease label
# PathFilter: StronglyTypedId package source only
# Interval  : poll every 10 minutes
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GitHub::Repository-Monitor CSharpPackage-StronglyTypedId-Main-Monitor
(
    Organization: BillHertzing,
    Repository: ATAP.Utilities,
    BranchFilter: main,
    PathFilter: src/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId/**,
    PollInterval: 600,
    WebhookSecret: $EnvironmentVariable(BUILDMASTER_GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET),
    PipelineName: CSharpPackage-5Stage,
    BuildVariables: %(Branch: $Branch,
                     ApplicationName: ATAP.Utilities,
                     MetaPackageName: ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId,
                     PackageName: ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId,
                     ProjectPath: src/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId.csproj,
                     SolutionPath: ATAP.Utilities.Production.slnf,
                     Configuration: Release)
);

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Monitor 2 — Sprint branches
# Triggers  : any push to a branch matching *-Sprint-*-work-items
# Starts    : Experimental deployment; ceiling still comes from version.json
# PathFilter: StronglyTypedId package source only
# Interval  : poll every 2 minutes
# Note      : pushes to the shared permanent nuget-experimental feed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GitHub::Repository-Monitor CSharpPackage-StronglyTypedId-Sprint-Monitor
(
    Organization: BillHertzing,
    Repository: ATAP.Utilities,
    BranchFilter: *-Sprint-*-work-items,
    PathFilter: src/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId/**,
    PollInterval: 120,
    WebhookSecret: $EnvironmentVariable(BUILDMASTER_GH_WEBHOOK_SECRET),
    PipelineName: CSharpPackage-5Stage,
    BuildVariables: %(Branch: $Branch,
                     ApplicationName: ATAP.Utilities,
                     MetaPackageName: ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId,
                     PackageName: ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId,
                     ProjectPath: src/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId/ATAP.Utilities.StronglyTypedId.csproj,
                     SolutionPath: ATAP.Utilities.Production.slnf,
                     Configuration: Release)
);

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Template — copy and adapt if per-package monitors are ever needed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
